+ * The retail game reads that from the animation's own flags (x597_bits, a fighter kind): when it
+ * is not the fighter's kind, the tracks are remapped onto the fighter's skeleton and the
+ * translation tracks of ordinary bones are dropped. A fighter m-ex adds carries the flags of the
+ * retail fighter its file was made from (Wolf's say Fox), although its animations are made for
+ * its own skeleton, every node with translation tracks first. m-ex therefore ignores the flags
+ * and asks who the animation belongs to (its "OwnsAnim" patches): the fighter's own animations
+ * are applied directly, and an animation played from another fighter's file (being thrown) is
+ * remapped from the shared thrown skeleton, the parts table entry after the last fighter.
+ * Fighter_ChangeMotionState records the owner in fp->mu_mex.anim_owner.
+ *
+ * Only the added fighters follow the m-ex rule here; a retail fighter keeps the retail test in
+ * every view. */
+static inline bool mu_ak_anim_rule(Fighter* fp)
+{
+    return MU_AK_KIND(fp->kind) && mu_mex_fighters_active();
